      "description": "• A how-to video on product usage that walks through several practical tips for operating a lotus-themed tabletop water fountain, covering noise fixes, leaf and flower adjustment, water flow control, pump gear settings, water level maintenance, and safe shutdown. • Pump noise (Tip A) can be resolved by toggling the switch off and on repeatedly to purge trapped air; the flowers, buds, and leaves (Tip B) are flexible and can be carefully repositioned by hand; placing small rocks at the first-level water outlet (Tip C) helps control the flow direction. • The fountain must be placed on a level surface (Tip D); the pump offers three flow gears with medium recommended (Tip E); water should be kept at an adequate level and replenished regularly (Tip F); and the switch should be turned off when leaving the fountain unattended to protect the pump (Tip G).",
